  "policy": "Every purchased component used in a capacity, geometry, collision, service, mass-property, life, accuracy, energy, or assembly claim shall use exactly one card and its matching component-catalogue record. Dimensions are fixed neutral equivalents, not manufacturer drawings. A candidate may design adapters, housings, couplings, fingers, pads, and structural parts around these cards, but may not substitute an unlisted purchased actuator, reducer, brake, bearing, gripper transmission, pneumatic device, or rating.",
  "geometryConvention": {
    "linearUnits": "mm",
    "massUnits": "kg",
    "inertiaUnits": "kg*m^2 about the local centre of mass, axes [Ixx,Iyy,Izz]",
    "axis": "Every card has a local right-handed XYZ frame. Z is the component axis; every named axial datum is a signed Z coordinate in that frame. The datum table, not an inferred drawing view, is authoritative for stack-up and service calculations.",
    "envelope": "Each primitive is an occupied conservative envelope. Interface pilots, shafts, bores, and bolt holes are exact connection features and are not occupied volume.",
    "tolerance": "Envelope dimensions are plus/minus 0.5 mm and mass/inertia values are plus/minus 10% unless the matching catalogue record states a larger uncertainty. Use the conservative envelope and catalogue derating for benchmark claims."
  },
